@startuml sequence-recommendations
' Menu Macro Fitter -- nearby restaurants, then recommendations (issue #37)
' Call order from backend/src/controllers/restaurants.js and recommendations.js. The student is already logged in.

skinparam defaultFontName Verdana
scale 2
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #999999
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam noteBorderColor #C9A227
autonumber

title Nearby Restaurants, Then Recommendations

participant "Client\n(web / mobile)" as Client
participant API
database MongoDB
participant "Overpass\n(OpenStreetMap)" as Overpass

== Find nearby restaurants ==
Client -> API : POST /api/restaurants/nearby\n{ lat, lng, radiusMiles? } + Bearer JWT
opt radiusMiles omitted
  API -> MongoDB : read user's saved searchRadius
end
API -> MongoDB : read all chain names
API -> Overpass : restaurants within radius\nwhose name contains a chain name
alt Overpass fails
  API --> Client : 502 "Places lookup failed"
else places found
  Overpass --> API : places (name, address, location)
  API -> API : sort by distance; match each\nplace name to a chain (or null)
  API --> Client : 200 { restaurants: [ ..., chainId ] }
end
note right of Client : the location is never stored

== Get recommendations ==
Client -> API : POST /api/recommendations\n{ chainIds, mode?, mealCalorieLimit? } + Bearer JWT
opt mode or mealCalorieLimit omitted
  API -> MongoDB : read user's profile and preferences
  API -> API : per-meal limit = saved limit,\nelse daily target / 3
  break no limit sent, no saved limit and no profile
    API --> Client : 400 "Set your profile first"
  end
end
API -> MongoDB : menu items at those chains,\n300 kcal to per-meal limit,\nnot estimated (unless includeEstimates)
API -> API : score = protein (or carb) grams\nper 100 kcal; sort; keep top 10 (default)
API --> Client : 200 { mode, mealCalorieLimit, items: [ ..., score ] }
Client -> Client : top third by score = "Great fit",\nthe rest = "OK"

@enduml
